# A two-part bracket, for the CI smoke render.
#
# Authored here rather than downloaded: it has to be redistributable without
# attribution questions, and it is more useful small than realistic. It does
# exercise the parts of the reader that matter — an unwelded quad mesh needing
# triangulation and welding, two `g` groups that become two parts, and a
# material library reference.
mtllib bracket.mtl

g Base
usemtl Steel
v -2.0 0.0 -1.0
v  2.0 0.0 -1.0
v  2.0 0.0  1.0
v -2.0 0.0  1.0
v -2.0 0.4 -1.0
v  2.0 0.4 -1.0
v  2.0 0.4  1.0
v -2.0 0.4  1.0
f 1 4 3 2
f 5 6 7 8
f 1 2 6 5
f 2 3 7 6
f 3 4 8 7
f 4 1 5 8

g Post
usemtl Anodized
v -0.4 0.4 -0.4
v  0.4 0.4 -0.4
v  0.4 0.4  0.4
v -0.4 0.4  0.4
v -0.4 2.2 -0.4
v  0.4 2.2 -0.4
v  0.4 2.2  0.4
v -0.4 2.2  0.4
f 9 12 11 10
f 13 14 15 16
f 9 10 14 13
f 10 11 15 14
f 11 12 16 15
f 12 9 13 16
